        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: साक्षीदार",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "साक्षीदार — sākṣīdār — \"a witness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "त्या साक्षीदाराने सगळं पाहिलं असतं तर त्याने पोलिसांना सांगितलं असतं. tyā sākṣīdārāne sagḷaṁ pāhilaṁ astaṁ tar tyāne polisānnā sāṅgitlaṁ astaṁ. If that witness had seen everything, he would have told the police."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "साक्षीदाराने, by the witness; a past form with असतं says what would have happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "साक्षीदार (sākṣīdār) is built from Sanskrit sākṣin, 'an eyewitness' (Monier-Williams), and the Persian suffix -dār, 'one who holds': the one who holds the testimony."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
