              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पाकीटमार — pākīṭmār — \"a pickpocket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गर्दीत एका पाकीटमाराने माझं पाकीट मारलं. gardīt ekā pākīṭmārāne mājhaṁ pākīṭ mārlaṁ. In the crowd a pickpocket stole my wallet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built from पाकीट, a wallet, and मार-, from मारणे: पाकीट मारणे, to pick a pocket."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पाकीटमार (pākīṭmār) is a Marathi compound built from pākīṭ, 'a wallet', a loan from English packet, and mār-, the stem of mārṇe, 'to strike' (CDIAL 10066)."
            }
          ]
